# Raw source data is NEVER committed.
# Safeguard S7 (raw data untouched) and S2 (no vendor or product names in the repo).
# Raw OMB files contain vendor and product columns. Committing them would break S2.
# The notebook re-downloads every raw file from its official URL and verifies its
# SHA-256 hash against governance/data-provenance.md, so results stay reproducible
# without the repo ever holding a vendor name.
data/raw/*
!data/raw/.gitkeep

# The vendor term list is built from raw data and lives in data/raw/ only.
vendor_terms*.txt
vendor_terms*.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS
.DS_Store

# The owner brief and the local editor configuration stay out of the repository.
# They describe how the work was done rather than what it found, which S11 keeps
# off the published record.
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
